From: RDK <rdk@rdkcentral.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: skip auth timeout registration when already in COMPLETED state

Block wpa_supplicant_req_auth_timeout from arming the authentication
timeout when the interface is already in WPA_COMPLETED state.

A spurious timeout registration while COMPLETED causes the 10-second
timer to fire and tear down an established mesh backhaul connection by
calling wpa_supplicant_deauthenticate() and clearing
NL80211_STA_FLAG_AUTHORIZED.

Root cause: after a successful SAE handshake on the mesh backhaul STA,
an unknown caller re-invokes wpa_supplicant_req_auth_timeout with a
10-second value while the interface is already COMPLETED.  The SAE
extended-timeout path does not override this because it only runs
during initial association, so the 10-second timer goes un-cancelled
and fires, tearing down the link.

---
 wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.c
@@ -258,6 +258,13 @@
 	if (wpa_s->conf->ap_scan == 0 &&
 	    (wpa_s->drv_flags & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS_WIRED))
 		return;
+	if (wpa_s->wpa_state == WPA_COMPLETED) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "Skip auth timeout registration (%d sec) "
+			   "- already in COMPLETED state on %s",
+			   sec, wpa_s->ifname);
+		return;
+	}
+
 
 	wpa_dbg(wpa_s, MSG_DEBUG, "Setting authentication timeout: %d sec "
 		"%d usec", sec, usec);
